{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"f8261e7939027c5248437964ba472b919756835557656469a57dc84913a03e56","packTokens":1274,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":205,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":419,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":545,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"How should authentication and authorization be applied to contract operations?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce authentication and authorization only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly declares them.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen if demo seeding runs more than once?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Repeated runs may insert duplicate copies of the sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"A pen may contain animals from multiple lots, but a feeding activity identifies a lot. How should a pen-level delivery be attributed when it serves multiple lots?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record a separate activity per lot, with each activity containing only that lot's share of the delivered feed.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What unit-conversion rule should be used when feed inventory, ration ingredients, and feeding quantities use different units?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Convert quantities to pounds for calculations and inventory deductions, treating a ton as 2,000 pounds; retain the entered units for display.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should implementation preserve any records that may already exist in the PostgreSQL App database while adding the contract's data model?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Preserve existing records and add the required model without resetting the database.\",\n  \"by\": \"hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement every operation in the locked OpenAPI contract, including its declared paths, methods, schemas, behavior, response codes, media types, and security rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement inventory, ration, feeding-plan, feeding-activity, weight-measurement, yard-summary, performance, report/export, administrator, synchronization, and demo operations as specified in the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Convert quantities and costs to pounds-based values using 2,000 pounds per ton, while retaining entered units in returned display values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feeding quantities, variances, consumption, costs, energy, inventory deductions, and lot allocations in pounds; represent multi-lot shares separately and attribute each share only to its lot.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate lot-performance metrics using the specified formulas, returning null or unavailable for undefined metrics while retaining other calculable metrics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Require bearer authentication and enforce role authorization only where declared by the contract, leaving sign-in unauthenticated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Persist contract-backed operational records in PostgreSQL through the configured App connection, and apply the data model without deleting, resetting, or changing existing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Run demo seeding only when Seed:Demo is true; populate contract tables with believable sample rows derived from contract examples, with repeated runs permitted to add duplicates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Configure the test factory to disable demo seeding unless explicitly opted in.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide the contract functionality through HTTP operations without adding feedlot product screens; exposed web routes are limited to API documentation or health information.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}